DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file + runtime-state gated command injection in lwan. Two conditions
  must hold: (1) exec_mode=1 in the --exec-config file, AND (2) /exec/init?token=
  must be called first. Input flows via exec_args_t struct to dispatch_exec() then
  system(). S3 metachar check exists but strict_exec=0 so it never activates.

CONFIG_GATE (C3 — config file + runtime state):
  mechanism:  key=value config file parsed by read_exec_config(); sets exec_cfg.enabled
              exec_initialized=0 global set to 1 by /exec/init?token= handler
  new arg:    --exec-config PATH added to getopt_long as short opt 'X'
  check:      `if (!exec_cfg.enabled || !exec_initialized) return HTTP_NOT_FOUND;`
  complexity: requires modelling both file I/O data flow AND inter-request HTTP state

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>
  path:       handle_exec() calls lwan_request_get_query_param(request, "cmd"),
              sets exec_args_t args={.cmd=cmd,.flags=0}, calls dispatch_exec(&args),
              which calls system(args->cmd)
  transforms: pointer through a struct and a helper function call

SANITIZATION (S3 — config-gated, never activated):
  check:   `if (strict_exec && strpbrk(cmd, "|;&\`$") != NULL)` — full metachar block
  bypass:  strict_exec is a static int initialized to 0; no mechanism sets it to 1.
           The check is structurally present but never reached in practice.

SINK:        system(args->cmd) in dispatch_exec() (src/bin/lwan/main.c)

